---
import Section from './Section.astro';
// The science layer — metrics from PRICING.md §1, each derived number naming the
// published method behind it. Named methods signal rigor better than adjectives.
// Honesty caveats (the readiness heuristic; no validated single sleep score) are
// stated as the docs require. no_validated_sleep_score is a real corpus note id.
const methods = [
  { metric: 'VO₂max (aerobic fitness)', method: 'Jurca non-exercise model + GPS submaximal' },
  { metric: 'Training load', method: 'Banister TRIMP · strain 0–21' },
  { metric: 'Sleep regularity', method: 'Phillips Sleep Regularity Index' },
  { metric: 'Biological age', method: 'Gompertz mortality model' },
  { metric: 'Max heart rate (for zones)', method: 'Tanaka age-predicted maximum' },
  { metric: 'Calories / energy', method: 'MET-by-state — never heart-rate guesses' },
  { metric: 'Sleep-health score', method: '4 parts, each scored on its own' },
  { metric: 'Illness early-warning', method: 'breathing-rate / skin-temp / HRV shifts' },
];

const vitals = [
  'Resting heart rate', 'Overnight HRV (heart-rate steadiness)', 'Blood oxygen (SpO₂)',
  'Breathing rate', 'Skin temperature', 'Stress (framed honestly)', 'Sleep stages & sleep debt',
  'Body clock (chronotype)', 'Active minutes vs target', 'Steps & distance', 'Weight / BMI',
  'GPS workouts + route',
];
---

<Section id="science" tone="sunk" labelledby="science-h">
  <h2 id="science-h" class="rise mt-4 max-w-2xl text-[clamp(1.9rem,4vw,3rem)]">
    No secret sauce. Every number uses a method you can look up.
  </h2>
  <p class="lede rise mt-6 max-w-2xl">
    Not a “proprietary algorithm.” Each number is computed with a published method, ported carefully
    and checked against known values — and if we can’t point to the research, we don’t compute it.
  </p>

  <div class="mt-10 grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[1.05fr_0.95fr] lg:gap-16">
    <div class="rise">
      <dl class="border-y border-line">
        {
          methods.map((m) => (
            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-1 border-t border-line py-3.5 first:border-t-0 sm:grid-cols-[11rem_1fr] sm:gap-4">
              <dt class="font-medium">{m.metric}</dt>
              <dd class="mono text-sm text-ink-soft">{m.method}</dd>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </dl>

      <p class="mt-6 text-[0.9rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-faint">
        Where a number is <em>ours</em>, we say so: the within-day readiness estimate is a plain rule
        of thumb, and no single “sleep score” is medically validated
        <span class="cite">[no_validated_sleep_score]</span>. The honesty points inward too.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="rise">
      <p class="eyebrow">Also tracked</p>
      <ul class="mt-5 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
        {vitals.map((v) => <li class="chip">{v}</li>)}
      </ul>

      <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
        <span class="chip chip-accent">Jurca</span>
        <span class="chip chip-accent">Banister TRIMP</span>
        <span class="chip chip-accent">Phillips SRI</span>
        <span class="chip chip-accent">Gompertz</span>
        <span class="chip chip-accent">Tanaka</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Section>
